{"h":3390,"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.016046683274890783,"t":"Test 4","w":0.063655033111572251,"x":0.094455850894590326,"c":1,"y":0.047965116370184302},{"h":0.016048398200741221,"x":0.094455849259598879,"y":0.095870206327330343,"c":1,"w":0.31211499532063802,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3"},{"h":0.017534472035095727,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","y":0.13362831863417324,"w":0.82546203613281244,"x":0.094455840144513553,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.17453798929850256,"t":"Passage 3 below.","y":0.14970930280592709,"h":0.019022260232660959,"x":0.092402463111455613},{"h":0.020490327908226247,"c":1,"w":0.29158111572265627,"t":"The Unselfish Gene","x":0.36755646460055708,"y":0.19026548619327399},{"h":0.017699115044247815,"c":1,"w":0.63449691772460937,"t":"A psychologist gives his view on how humans became self-centred","y":0.23097345148128956,"x":0.19507186958865211},{"c":1,"h":0.01749245410120237,"x":0.092402473770623883,"w":0.80492813110351569,"y":0.26598837190116931,"t":"There has long been a general assumption that human beings are essentially selfish."},{"y":0.28488372142214136,"t":"We're apparently ruthless, with strong impulses to compete against each other for","x":0.09240246938592217,"h":0.018951086308752307,"c":1,"w":0.77412729899088539},{"y":0.3023255814188992,"h":0.017441860412777732,"c":1,"t":"resources and to accumulate power and possessions. If we are kind to one another, it's","x":0.092402471082273605,"w":0.8234086100260416},{"w":0.79260777791341142,"t":"usually because we have ulterior motives. If we are good, it's only because we have","x":0.09240247644370489,"y":0.321220930348036,"h":0.015988371857499573,"c":1},{"h":0.016008094630058589,"x":0.092402466114861526,"y":0.33864306803998079,"c":1,"w":0.66735112508138017,"t":"managed to control and transcend our innate selfishness and brutality."},{"x":0.092402474313385885,"h":0.016224188790560423,"y":0.37345132716853369,"c":1,"w":0.72689936319986981,"t":"This bleak view of human nature is closely associated with the science writer"},{"h":0.016224188790560534,"w":0.8234086100260416,"c":1,"t":"Richard Dawkins, whose 1976 book The Selfish Gene became popular because it fitted","y":0.3923303836489227,"x":0.094455859155357022},{"y":0.4098837210446773,"c":1,"t":"so well with - and helped to justify - the competitive and individualistic ethos that was","h":0.016074981239341257,"w":0.8069815063476562,"x":0.09240247054365644},{"c":1,"x":0.09240246496505837,"h":0.017512176873761276,"y":0.4273255814167265,"w":0.8295687866210939,"t":"so prevalent in late 20th-century societies. Like many others, Dawkins justifies his views"},{"c":1,"y":0.44476744171221583,"x":0.092402467921485917,"w":0.82956878662109368,"t":"with reference to the field of evolutionary psychology. Evolutionary psychology theorises","h":0.017474446254493903},{"t":"that present-day human traits developed in prehistoric times, during what is termed the","x":0.092402451797879717,"y":0.46366279072152428,"h":0.017458153333635762,"c":1,"w":0.81724848429361963},{"t":"'environment of evolutionary adaptedness'.","y":0.47964601747224922,"w":0.41273101806640627,"c":1,"x":0.090349069917484329,"h":0.017447005752968536},{"w":0.77618067423502601,"h":0.017501028730454338,"c":1,"t":"Prehistory is usually seen as a period of intense competition, when life was such a","x":0.09240247593413263,"y":0.51592920379876483},{"x":0.092402458469465029,"w":0.82751541137695317,"h":0.016063833096034319,"y":0.53480825980726343,"c":1,"t":"brutal battle that only those with traits such as selfishness, aggression and ruthlessness"},{"t":"survived. And because survival depended on access to resources - such as rivers,","x":0.092308064257362904,"y":0.54924680457944552,"w":0.78257939656575504,"h":0.020555038227092481,"c":1},{"h":0.017548192567178322,"x":0.09034907656215467,"c":1,"w":0.82135523478190109,"y":0.56976744188406192,"t":"forests and animals - there was bound to be conflict between rival groups, which led to"},{"x":0.09240247719178124,"w":0.80903488159179671,"c":1,"h":0.018963949377909461,"t":"the development of traits such as racism and warfare. This seems logical. But, in fact,","y":0.5857558144417071},{"y":0.60459888036275544,"t":"the assumption on which this all rests - that prehistoric life was a desperate struggle for","w":0.8276047770182291,"x":0.092360252499275264,"c":1,"h":0.018906491484965482},{"t":"survival — is false.","x":0.092038817870933279,"y":0.6210109923944872,"w":0.17339997609456381,"h":0.018707762636617886,"c":1},{"t":"It's important to remember that in the prehistoric era, the world was very sparsely","h":0.017465013599677004,"c":1,"y":0.65840707939428367,"w":0.75564682006835937,"x":0.092402462523281964},{"w":0.79055440266927068,"h":0.016027817402617384,"c":1,"t":"populated. According to some estimates, around 15,000 years ago, the population of","y":0.67728613596573461,"x":0.092402470029591566},{"y":0.69469026571989867,"w":0.77823410034179674,"x":0.094455845001425676,"t":"Europe was only 29,000, and the population of the whole world was less than half a","h":0.017519036577162805,"c":1},{"w":0.78850102742513029,"c":1,"y":0.71209439509474715,"t":"million. Humans at that time were hunter-gatherers: people who lived by hunting wild","x":0.09240246360785212,"h":0.016224188790560423},{"x":0.09240246490166508,"w":0.8295687866210939,"t":"animals and collecting wild plants. With such small population densities, it seems unlikely","y":0.73097345157395455,"h":0.016224188790560534,"c":1},{"x":0.092402464625440647,"h":0.01605525790414275,"t":"that prehistoric hunter-gatherer groups had to compete against each other for resources","w":0.82135523478190098,"y":0.74854651174333808,"c":1},{"y":0.7659883721164239,"h":0.017492454101202481,"x":0.092402468187673129,"t":"or had any need to develop ruthlessness and competitiveness, or to go to war.","w":0.73305953979492189,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.092402456319170961,"h":0.015988371857499573,"y":0.80087209313733376,"t":"There is significant evidence to back this notion from contemporary hunter-gatherer","w":0.76180699666341156},{"t":"groups, who live in the same way as prehistoric humans did. As the anthropologist","w":0.75154001871744791,"h":0.017466727962887729,"c":1,"x":0.092402478444150796,"y":0.81828908579001269},{"x":0.092360849872908754,"w":0.80709325154622402,"t":"Bruce Knauft has remarked, hunter-gatherers are characterised by 'extreme political and","y":0.83528445076365332,"h":0.019990231224217614,"c":1},{"t":"sexual egalitarianism'. Knauft has observed that individuals in such groups don't accumulate","x":0.092402466890791568,"y":0.85309734491907085,"h":0.017542189764062188,"c":1,"w":0.8316221618652343},{"w":0.82144276936848959,"c":1,"x":0.09236706021266021,"y":0.87066466663319153,"t":"property or possessions and have an ethical obligation to share everything. They also have","h":0.019083190737924083},{"h":0.017544762152837734,"c":1,"y":0.8895348837432745,"w":0.77002054850260415,"t":"methods of preserving egalitarianism by ensuring that disparities of status don't arise.","x":0.092402456705774988},{"y":0.92441860489760386,"x":0.092402464803064077,"w":0.026694043477376306,"t":"92","c":1,"h":0.013081394746943587},{"y":0.94166666659226195,"w":0.45882354736328124,"c":1,"h":0.04166666666666663,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.51176469619230891}]}